For each of these operations, the function creates temporary tables and executes the corresponding SQL query for each `SELECT` statement involved in the operation. It then merges or intersects the results based on the operation type. Finally, it releases any allocated resources and returns the final result.

The function also includes a section to compute collating sequences used by the temporary tables needed to implement the compound select. This is only run by the right-most `SELECT` statement if there are temporary tables required and no ORDER BY clause exists. The computed collating sequences are attached to all temporary tables created during the query execution.

