3. Use After Free (CWE-789): The code dynamically allocates memory for `name` and then deletes it after setting the handler name. If an exception is thrown before the deletion occurs, or if the same block of memory is reused without proper deallocation, a use-after-free vulnerability could arise. Confidence: Low
