3. Potential Information Disclosure (CWE-200) - The code displays the output of a "who" command when the function is called with an invalid channel (i.e., no valid channel or the checking_whox counter for the channel is less than 0). This might inadvertently disclose information about other users and their statuses. To mitigate this issue, you can restrict who and similar commands to be executed only when the function is called with a valid channel.
   - Confidence: Low

