In terms of severity and exploitability, the shell injection vulnerability (CWE-88) is considered high because it can lead to arbitrary command execution on the server. The exposure of sensitive information could be medium-severity, depending on what exactly is being exposed and how easily an attacker could access or use this information for malicious purposes.

