- Implement secure password storage practices using hashing and salting.
- Use parameterized queries to prevent SQL injection.
- Validate all user input thoroughly to prevent cross-site scripting and other types of attacks.
- Improve session management and ensure that sensitive data is handled securely.
- Handle exceptions and errors in a way that does not mask security-related issues.
- Implement secure cookies and ensure proper handling of user sessions.

