Additionally, there is no error handling or validation for user-provided data. Specifically, there are no checks to prevent maliciously crafted `message` strings from causing issues with the log functionality. This opens up opportunities for potential attacks such as command injection if `message` is treated as executable code at any point in the application.
</analysis>

