#### CWE-134 (Use of Externally-Controlled Format String)

The `cp += label_len` operation can be interpreted as a format string vulnerability if the attacker controls the `label_len` value. This could potentially lead to unexpected behavior or even crashes.

#### CWE-131 (Incorrect Calculation of Buffer Size) - LOW CONFIDENCE

The function calculates buffer sizes based on user-controlled input (`packet`, `length`). While this might not be directly exploitable, it's essential to ensure proper buffer sizing to prevent potential issues.

